# D-105 native, the result route (steps/d105-native.md §5): a result passed
# through a result: `id2 (Model: m) Model` returns `id(m)`, whose result carries Other; the edges run
# formal -> result -> result -> formal, and `rd(id2(o))` reads 10.  Success is 7.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    size_t: b 2U
end: Model
Other:
    size_t: b 20U
    size_t: a 10U
end: Other
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: id (Model: m) Model
return: m
fn: id2 (Model: m) Model
return: id(m)
fn: go () size_t
    o: merge: Other
    return: rd(id2(o))
size_t: got 0U
got: go()
int: ok 3
if: got = 10U
    ok: 7
if: got = 20U
    ok: 5
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
